Package: SeMiLLa
Type: Package
Title: SEmantic Measurement of Items via LLM Assistance
Version: 2.10.0
Date: 2026-10-08
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jose", "Ventura-Leon",
           email = "jventuraleon@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-2996-4244"))
    )
Description: Drafts psychometric scale items from a psychological construct
    with Large Language Models (LLMs) and audits them before any data are
    collected. It derives a working definition and dimensions from the model's
    knowledge, from user input or from 'PubMed' and 'Semantic Scholar'
    abstracts; writes items; obtains text embeddings; and checks whether items
    of the same dimension group together by ensemble clustering of those
    embeddings (semantic separability, not factor analysis of responses). A
    pre-administration gate simulates ordinal responses under stated
    assumptions about loadings, factor correlations and social desirability,
    and simulated LLM judges rate content validity (Aiken's V). These checks
    describe the wording, not the behaviour of real respondents, and do not
    replace a field study.
